  "question": "The mass of a planet is $\\dfrac{1}{10}$th that of the earth and its diameter is half that of the earth. The acceleration due to gravity on that planet is :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$4.9\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$3.92\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$19.6\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$9.8\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$g = \\dfrac{GM}{R^2}$, so\n$$g_p = g\\cdot\\frac{M_p}{M}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{R}{R_p}\\right)^2 = 9.8 \\times \\frac{1}{10} \\times 2^2 = 3.92\\ \\text{m s}^{-2}$$",
